quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  20,88,"Then, he (Samiri) produced for them (from the molten jewellery) a statue of a calf, with a lowing sound (of a cow). Then they said: ‘This is your god and Musa’s god, but he forgot (to mention).’"
  20,89,"Could they not see that it (i.e. the calf) would not respond to them with speech, and that it did not possess for them (any) harm or benefit?"
  20,90,And Harun (Aaron) had already told them: ‘O my people! You are only being tested by it. And surely your Lord is the Most-Compassionate. So follow me and obey my command.’
  20,91,They said: ‘We shall not cease to be its devotees until Musa (Moses) returns to us.’
  20,92,"He (Musa [Moses]) said: ‘O Harun (Aaron)! What prevented you when you saw them going astray,"
  20,93,from coming after me (to inform me)? Did you disobey my command?’
  20,94,"He (Aaron) said: ‘O son of my mother! Do not hold my beard or my head. I was scared you would say: ‘You have caused division among the Children of Israel, and you did not wait for my word.’’"
  20,95,"He (Musa [Moses]) said: ‘What was your purpose, O Samiri?’"
  20,96,"He said: ‘I saw what they had not seen (i.e. the Archangel Gabriel). I took a handful (of dust) from the messenger’s footprints (from when he visited you), and then I threw it (in the gold casting for the calf). That is how my soul prompted me.’"
  20,97,"He (Musa [Moses]) said (to Samiri): ‘Get away (from here). It shall be for you (a punishment) in this life to keep saying: ‘Don’t touch me!’ And there is yet another promise (of punishment), which you will never be allowed to escape. Now, look at your god, which you have kept on worshipping. We shall surely burn it down and then scatter it into the sea like dust."
  20,98,"(O my people!) Indeed, your God is only Allah. There is no god except Him. He comprehends everything in (His) knowledge.’"
